+For the $\rho=1/4$ symmetric paired second coordinate, the primary
+interval excludes exact zero while remaining inside the resolution band.
+Both its Bonferroni-$t$ interval and the restricted-grid interval include
+zero. In this symmetric-noise setting, the objective and updates are
+invariant under reflection of the second coordinate, so the ideal
+finite-time second-coordinate mean from zero initial states is zero.
+The small interval exclusion is therefore not evidence of a nonzero
+second-order coefficient. Exact-zero inclusion and resolution within a
+specified margin are distinct conclusions.
