+First/last-half balance comparisons have eight nominal 95\% exclusions
+among 144 scalar diagnostics, all for individual algorithms. None of the
+paired comparisons excludes zero, but this does not establish
+stationarity. Direct-mean estimates have substantially larger sampling
+variation than balance estimates. Finite-window update identities check
+time alignment and arithmetic, not stationary approximation; grid,
